Game data
---------

No SEGA data is included: no disc image, executable, overlay, texture, model, motion, sound, music, generated assembly
or recorded game memory. The build extracts what it needs from the user's own disc image of Sonic Adventure (USA)
v1.005 on the user's machine. Sonic Adventure, Sonic the Hedgehog and the characters are trademarks of SEGA; this
project is not affiliated with or endorsed by SEGA.

Third-party material and credits
--------------------------------

* Symbol names in sadc/config were seeded from the SA Tools (X-Hax) data-label configurations for the Dreamcast
  release, from the Sonic Adventure DX and Sonic Adventure 2 (Dreamcast, Exant64's sa2dc) symbol research and from the
  Katana SDK's documented function names; names are facts about the game and are listed without their sources' data.
* libsa1/src/sa1_audio_mix.c: the AICA envelope rate tables (attack / decay times) are the values published in the
  SCSP / AICA hardware documentation, as also used by MAME's aica.cpp; no MAME code is included.
* The Hitachi SH C compiler (SHC), Ghidra and the JDK are NOT included: the matching build uses the user's own copy of
  SHC 5.1r03 (sadc/tools/shc/, see sadc/README.md); Ghidra is optional.
* The SH-4 instruction decoder, the PRS codec, the splitter and the harness are this project's own code.
